Title: Can't select deleted company as current party

Description:
### Description of the bug

There are several apps that require support for submitting instances for deleted companies. This was supported in Altinn 2. There should be no blockage of this in authorization, and it seems it's strictly a problem in the app frontend code.

Seems we need to fix our party selector to allow choosing deleted companies if the app has been configures to allow it. We can probably add the config next to partyTypesAllowed in applicationMetadata.json.

Reported by Advokattilsynet [here](https://github.com/Altinn/altinn-support-private/issues/3981)

https://altinn.slack.com/archives/C02EJ9HKQA3/p1738657491966419

### Steps To Reproduce

1. Have a person that has a role in a deleted company.
2. Try to create a new instance of an app that has allowed party types set to company.
3. Observe that the application claims that the user doesn't have access to a company that can create the instance.

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03f0bb80-5c4d-469d-be65-f9cee4278458)

### Additional Information

It seems like this is the code that filters out the deleted company: 

`partyProviderUtils.ts`
```export const reduceToValidParties = (parties: IParty[], partyTypesAllowed: IPartyTypesAllowed): IParty[] => {
  const allParties = flattenParties(parties);

  const partyTypeFilters: { [key in PartyType]: boolean } = {
    [PartyType.Organisation]: partyTypesAllowed.organisation,
    [PartyType.SubUnit]: partyTypesAllowed.subUnit,
    [PartyType.Person]: partyTypesAllowed.person,
    [PartyType.SelfIdentified]: partyTypesAllowed.person, // Self-identified is treated as a person
    [PartyType.BankruptcyEstate]: partyTypesAllowed.bankruptcyEstate,
  };

  // Fun fact: If all party types are false then all are true
  if (Object.values(partyTypeFilters).every((value) => !value)) {
    return allParties.filter((party) => !party.isDeleted && !party.onlyHierarchyElementWithNoAccess);
  }

  return allParties.filter(
    (party) => !party.isDeleted && !party.onlyHierarchyElementWithNoAccess && partyTypeFilters[party.partyTypeName],
  );
};```

Source: https://github.com/Altinn/app-frontend-react/issues/2912

