Title: Cannot clear field if data is invalid

Description:
### Description of the bug

If the data is invalid, and you try to clear it. It will call setValue with an empty string. This will remove the value in the currentData, but does nothing to the invalid data object. This causes the invalid data to get "stuck".

https://github.com/Altinn/app-frontend-react/assets/47412359/f8470338-784c-4ef8-8119-0a624d364e4d


The problem is in this section:

`FormDataWriteStateMachine.tsx`
```ts
    if (newValue === '' || newValue === null || newValue === undefined) {
      dot.delete(path, state.currentData);
    } else {
      const schema = schemaLookup.getSchemaForPath(path)[0];
      const { newValue: convertedValue, error } = convertData(newValue, schema);
      if (error) {
        dot.delete(path, state.currentData);
        dot.str(path, newValue, state.invalidCurrentData);
      } else {
        dot.delete(path, state.invalidCurrentData);
        dot.str(path, convertedValue, state.currentData);
      }
    }

```

### Steps To Reproduce

.

### Additional Information

_No response_

Source: https://github.com/Altinn/app-frontend-react/issues/1679

