2. And validate the radio button labels.
3. The label seems to: Prioriterer du å bruke tid på skolearbeidet (både arbeid i timene og lekser)? op-2941
4. You can see the option id is in the label which it should not.


### Additional Information

After searching around in the code it seems to be something wronge in the LikertComponent.tsx:

```typescript
<RadioButton
  aria-labelledby={`${rowLabelId} ${colLabelId}`}
  checked={isChecked}
  onChange={handleChange}
  value={option.value}
  label={`${getPlainTextFromNode(text)} ${option.label}`}
  hideLabel={true}
  name={rowLabelId}
  radioId={inputId}
  error={!isValid}
/>;
```
First of all RadioButton in digdir doesn't have aria-labelledby prop. So the label used will be the label prop. Seen in the label prop it doesn't look up the option with the getTextResources function.

Source: https://github.com/Altinn/app-frontend-react/issues/705

